# Optional: enables the one AI fallback in enrichment -- classifying a
# ticket's taxonomy "system area" tag when the deterministic rule engine
# (services/enricher.py) detected no domain at all for it. Constrained to
# a fixed, closed set of area values (models/enrichment.py's SystemArea
# enum) via Anthropic tool-use, so it can never mint a new tag. Without
# this key, an unclassified ticket's area just stays "unknown" -- nothing
# else in the system depends on this, and it never affects routing
# (routing only ever reads the rule-based `domains`, never `system_areas`).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional: only needed for Arcade integration (Phase 3).
# ARCADE_API_KEY=
# ARCADE_GATEWAY_URL=

# Optional: lets the web portal (support-portal) actually create a real
# Linear issue and post a real Slack message for AUTO-tier recommended
# actions right after classifying a ticket, via Arcade's tool-execution
# API. Without ARCADE_API_KEY, the portal still classifies tickets fully
# — it just reports those two actions as skipped rather than executing
# them. ARCADE_USER_ID identifies you (support engineering) to Arcade for
# authorization purposes, not the customer submitting the ticket — the
# first classify call for each action will return a one-time
# authorization link if that user hasn't granted Linear/Slack access yet.
# LINEAR_TEAM and SLACK_CHANNEL must be a real team/channel in whatever
# workspace you've connected — this repo's routing policy names
# (identity-integrations, support-engineering) are illustrative, not
# literal Linear/Slack identifiers. SLACK_CHANNEL without a leading '#'.
# ARCADE_API_KEY=
# ARCADE_USER_ID=support-portal
# LINEAR_TEAM=
# SLACK_CHANNEL=
